      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how the math of the cosmos makes your struggle feel pointless, and I want to tell you that the very act of trying to keep the struggle going is already a rebellion against the void. The universe may eventually erase everything, but the fact that you are still fighting the void, still choosing to keep the play going, is the only thing that gives it meaning. You don't need to find a grand, eternal purpose to make your pain matter; you only need to keep the story alive for a little while longer. Let's keep talking about how you can make that next day feel a bit less heavy.",
